$ .venv/bin/python scripts/import_user_protections.py --help
usage: import_user_protections.py [-h] --ods ODS --expected-sha256
                                  EXPECTED_SHA256 [--sheet SHEET]
                                  [--base-policy BASE_POLICY]
                                  [--bundle-output BUNDLE_OUTPUT]
                                  [--policy-output POLICY_OUTPUT]
                                  [--provenance-output PROVENANCE_OUTPUT]
                                  [--bundle-id BUNDLE_ID]
                                  [--window-version WINDOW_VERSION]
                                  [--policy-id POLICY_ID]
                                  [--protection-prefix PROTECTION_PREFIX]
                                  [--check]

Strictly import the user's 35-word protection sheet into a versioned bundle,
pair policy and provenance. Only stored cell values are read: formulas, empty
or non-numeric cells, non-finite values, duplicate/unknown/missing words, any
content outside the declared range and display text that differs from the
stored value are all rejected. Frames use zero-based inclusive outward
rounding [floor(start*30), ceil(end*30)], computed with Decimal and cross-
checked with the float rule of the existing loader. Outputs are never
overwritten; --check rebuilds them in memory and compares bytes.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --ods ODS             Repository-relative ODS copy
  --expected-sha256 EXPECTED_SHA256
  --sheet SHEET
  --base-policy BASE_POLICY
  --bundle-output BUNDLE_OUTPUT
  --policy-output POLICY_OUTPUT
  --provenance-output PROVENANCE_OUTPUT
  --bundle-id BUNDLE_ID
  --window-version WINDOW_VERSION
  --policy-id POLICY_ID
  --protection-prefix PROTECTION_PREFIX
  --check               Rebuild in memory and compare with existing outputs
exit 0
$ .venv/bin/python scripts/preflight_hospital35.py --help
usage: preflight_hospital35.py [-h] [--policy POLICY] --output OUTPUT

Preflight every protected core and both endpoint roles before a library-wide
pair run. Global input blockers, intrinsic protected-source defects (speed,
joint limit, coupling and sampled geometry; acceleration and jerk inside cores
are informational as in v5) and words without a usable exit or entry endpoint
are reported separately. Budget exhaustion is INCOMPLETE, never a pass.
Predicted pair impacts are diagnostics only; pairs are still planned and
verified.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --policy POLICY
  --output OUTPUT  New directory; never reused
exit 0
$ .venv/bin/python scripts/run_hospital35_batches.py --help
usage: run_hospital35_batches.py [-h]
                                 {pairs,recheck-pairs,sequences,aggregate} ...

Single-writer, soft-budget driver for frozen hospital35 pair batches and sequence sub-batches.

pairs          plan then independently review frozen pair batches (<=16 pairs) in one run
recheck-pairs  fresh verify_saved_pair_v2 of every selected candidate into a new directory
sequences      plan and recheck one frozen sequence sub-batch (<=8 cases) into its registered output
aggregate      merge registered sequence outputs into a fixed-denominator table

Budgets are checked only at saved breakpoints, so a stop is soft. Every
invocation appends a new log with command, limits, resources and exit code.

positional arguments:
  {pairs,recheck-pairs,sequences,aggregate}
    pairs               Frozen pair batches in one single-writer run
    recheck-pairs       Fresh independent recheck of selected pair candidates

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
exit 0
