$ .venv/bin/python scripts/plan_sequences.py --help
usage: plan_sequences.py [-h] [--sequence-policy SEQUENCE_POLICY]
                         --pair-run-dir PAIR_RUN_DIR --output OUTPUT
                         [--case CASES] [--case-budget-s CASE_BUDGET_S]
                         [--soft-wall-time-s SOFT_WALL_TIME_S]
                         [--min-free-gib MIN_FREE_GIB]
                         [--resume-from RESUME_FROM]

Assemble frozen multi-word cases from one independently verified pair run,
then verify each saved chain. Each case first checks its pair dependencies
(not planned, planning or review unfinished, no numerical candidate) and is
recorded as BLOCKED_DEPENDENCY instead of stopping the run; a stale or corrupt
pair run still stops everything. Soft budgets (per case including
verification, per invocation wall clock, free disk) are checked before each
attempt: unstarted cases stay NOT_RUN and an interrupted attempt is never
selected. --resume-from reads earlier outputs of the same identity: their
passing selections are retained, their completely verified attempts are not
repeated and all files stay.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --sequence-policy SEQUENCE_POLICY
  --pair-run-dir PAIR_RUN_DIR
  --output OUTPUT       New directory; never reused
  --case CASES          Sequence id from the frozen policy; may repeat
  --case-budget-s CASE_BUDGET_S
                        Soft per-case budget, planning plus verification
  --soft-wall-time-s SOFT_WALL_TIME_S
  --min-free-gib MIN_FREE_GIB
  --resume-from RESUME_FROM
                        Earlier output of the same identity, in order; read
                        only
exit 0
$ .venv/bin/python scripts/verify_sequences.py --help
usage: verify_sequences.py [-h] --run-dir RUN_DIR

Fresh independent recheck of every selected saved sequence; recounts cases,
occurrences and connectors from files. Every case of the output keeps its row.
Blocked, incomplete, not-run and unselected cases are counted separately and
never as a pass or as agreement; a selection retained from an earlier output
is rechecked there, not here.

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --run-dir RUN_DIR
exit 0
